==Sanskrit==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ine-pro|sa}} {{m|ine-pro|*bʰruHg-||to enjoy}}.

===Noun===
{{sa-noun|tr=phála|g=n}}

# [[fruit]]
# the kernel or seed of a fruit
# a [[nutmeg]]
# the menstrual discharge
# {{label|sa|figuratively}} fruit, consequence, effect, result, retribution (good or bad), gain or loss, reward or punishment, advantage or disadvantage
# [[benefit]], [[enjoyment]]
# [[compensation]]
# {{label|sa|rhetoric}} the issue or end of an action
# {{label|sa|mathematics}} the result of a calculation, product or quotient
# corrective equation
# area or superficial contents of a figure
# interest on capital
# the third term in a rule of three sum
# [[gift]], [[donation]]
# a gaming board
# a blade (of a sword or knife)
# the point of an arrow
# [[shield]]
# a ploughshare
# a point or spot on a die

====Declension====
{{sa-decl-noun-a-n|फ|ल|phá|l}}

